# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# uv
.uv-cache/

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# IDE
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Project-specific
*.log
local/
scratch/

# Model-comparison console logs are deliberately TRACKED evidence (Cray, typed
# 2026-08-28: keep the logs — local LLM capability is a standing selling point and
# swapping in new models has to stay a measured decision). They are the ONLY place
# the latency aggregates and the DEADLINE breach line live; the JSONL dumps carry
# per-item numbers but not those. Without this negation the *.log rule above
# silently drops half of every comparison's evidence.
!benchmarks/model_compare/evidence/*.log

# Ontology codegen outputs (ADR-008 D5; reproducible from <name>_v0.yaml)
verticals/*/generated/
# Shared/core ontology codegen outputs (ADR-0033 D5; the committed shared ORM
# lands at services/db/person.py, NOT here — the reference artifacts are gitignored).
ontology/generated/

# Strategy (confidential — see ADR-006 D2)
# Company-specific opportunity analysis, design partner names, deal structure.
# Public abstract strategy lives in docs/strategy/public/.
docs/strategy/private/

# Research (working notes — Tier 0 Cowork output, gitignored)
# Cowork research briefs + closeouts. Code tab may lift edited
# versions to docs/strategy/public/ in a future batch.
docs/research/private/

# Docker
.docker/

# Node (future frontend)
node_modules/
.next/

# Claude Code local harness config
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code per-machine state (loop counters, session markers, tokens)
# Phase 1 (PLAN-0007) registers the directory; Phase 2 populates loop-counter.json.
.claude/state/

# Step 5b config-file fallback for the Sonnet classifier — belt-and-suspenders.
# The canonical location is ~/.claude/.anthropic_api_key (outside repo); this
# project-local entry blocks accidental commits if a developer places it inside.
.claude/.anthropic_api_key

# Per-machine dev-server launch configs. Credential-shaped by construction: a
# published-profile entry carries UI_DEMO_PERSONA_KEYS (person_id -> RAW key),
# and a local one can carry whatever the operator was holding at the time.
# The demo personas are synthetic and their keys are browser-served by ruling
# (PLAN-0103 SD-4 / the s224 credential ruling), so the exposure is not what
# makes this an entry — the FILE CLASS is: an un-ignored credential-shaped file
# in a public repo is one `git add -A` away from a commit, and the next value
# placed here may not be synthetic.
.claude/launch.json

# PLAN-0010 loop — messages are uncommitted by design (producer has no git
# per K-1; consumer processes in place then archives to processed/).
# Directory layout + schema specced in docs/plans/done/0010-step1-message-schema.md.
loop/inbox/*
loop/processed/*
!loop/inbox/.gitkeep
!loop/processed/.gitkeep
# Dispatcher local state (failure counts per message; regenerates on each run).
loop/.failures.json
loop/.failures.json.tmp

# Probe code (PLAN-0012 OQ-B probe — capability-restricted by contract;
# DO NOT promote to production; remove from tree after probe cleanup).
tools/probes/

# PLAN-0096 Step 2 — repair-case photo uploads (settings.repair_case_photo_dir,
# default var/repair-case-photos). USER CONTENT, and this repo is PUBLIC: a photo
# of a garage quote carries the vendor's name, the amount, sometimes a person.
# Assume it is PII (CLAUDE.md §8 PDPA) and keep it structurally uncommittable —
# the ignore rule is the guard, not the discipline of whoever runs .
var/

# Raw benchmark dumps (PLAN-0104 Step 7 and any successor run under .claude/).
# UNTRACKED-BUT-PRESENT is the hazard, not the content: this repo is PUBLIC, the
# directory sits inside a tree people `git add -A` from, and nothing in history
# protects a file that has never been committed. Same FILE CLASS as
# `.claude/launch.json` above — an un-ignored, un-reviewed artifact one careless
# stage away from a public commit.
#
# Not hypothetical: a malformed shell command in session 231 staged all 78 files
# in one go. It was caught and unstaged, but only because someone happened to be
# reading `git status` at that moment. The ignore rule is the guard; whoever
# remembers is not.
#
# This entry is also the durable HOME for the warning that until now lived only
# in a STATUS Active-TODO row (the R2 carve-out, session 231). The fact is now a
# mechanism, so that row can be trimmed on its normal schedule.
.claude/benchmark-results/

# Personal brand marks (the Cray.J wordmark + mascot) — NOT a vero-lite asset.
# This repo is PUBLIC and Apache 2.0, so an image committed here inherits that
# licence grant. A personal wordmark is not something to hand out under it by
# accident, and nothing in the product needs it.
#
# `docs/design/Cray_J_v1_small.png` sat UNTRACKED-BUT-PRESENT for six sessions
# (first seen 2026-08-06). It was an orphan by measurement, not by impression:
# `git grep -i Cray_J_v1` over the whole tree returned rc=1, zero hits — nothing
# tracked referenced it, and `docs/design/` otherwise holds only .md files. What
# it did cost was a line of attention at every session close — notice the dirty
# tree, confirm it is not this session's work, then write a "do not commit"
# warning into the handoff, six times over.
#
# Same FILE CLASS as `.claude/benchmark-results/` above: an un-ignored artifact
# one careless `git add -A` from a public commit. The ignore rule is the guard;
# whoever remembers is not. A clean `git status` is also what lets the NEXT
# unexpected file actually read as unexpected.
#
# Ruled by Cray (typed, session 247): ignore rather than commit or delete — the
# file stays where it is on disk and simply stops being the repo's problem. The
# pattern is family-wide rather than filename-exact because `v1_small` implies
# siblings (other versions, other sizes) that would otherwise land right back here.
docs/design/Cray_J_*
